TITLE:: PatternChip
SUMMARY:: Labelled chip for one sequence in the Arranger.
CATEGORIES:: GUI>Views
RELATED:: Classes/Arranger, Classes/BorderView, Classes/Sequencer

DESCRIPTION::
TELETYPE::PatternChip:: is a LINK::Classes/BorderView:: that LINK::Classes/Arranger:: places for each sequence. It stores that sequence's LINK::Classes/Symbol:: id, the same id LINK::Classes/Sequencer:: uses, and shows it as a centred LINK::Classes/StaticText::. The chip uses LINK::Classes/GuiPalette#-colour3:: as its fill and LINK::Classes/GuiPalette#-colour4:: as its border colour. The border width is 1 and the corner radius is 5. A left double-click calls LINK::Classes/Sequencer#-play:: with that id and looping on. Double-clicking the chip for the id that is already playing calls LINK::Classes/Sequencer#-stop::. LINK::#-applyPlaying:: sets the border to LINK::Classes/GuiPalette#-extreme2:: while that id is playing, and restores LINK::Classes/GuiPalette#-colour4:: otherwise. A left click calls LINK::#-clickAction_::. A left-button drag that travels more than 4 pixels moves the chip, brings it to the front, and keeps it inside its parent. Releasing the button calls LINK::#-dragAction_:: with the chip's origin. A click that became a drag does not call LINK::#-clickAction_::. A double-click stays under that threshold and still toggles playback. Ctrl+left-click, released without dragging, calls LINK::#-openAction_:: and does not select or toggle playback. Ctrl+drag still drags and does not open.

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
Creates a TELETYPE::PatternChip:: and adds it to CODE::parent::.

ARGUMENT:: parent
The LINK::Classes/View:: that holds the chip.

ARGUMENT:: sequencer
The LINK::Classes/Sequencer:: that plays this chip's sequence.

ARGUMENT:: sequenceId
The LINK::Classes/Symbol:: that identifies the sequence, displayed with CODE::asString::.

RETURNS::
A new TELETYPE::PatternChip:: instance.

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: clickAction_
Called when a left click is released without becoming a drag. CODE::nil:: clears it.

ARGUMENT:: action
A LINK::Classes/Function:: or CODE::nil::. The function is called with no arguments.

METHOD:: dragAction_
Called with the chip's origin when a drag is released. CODE::nil:: clears it.

ARGUMENT:: action
A LINK::Classes/Function:: or CODE::nil::. The function receives one LINK::Classes/Point::, the chip's parent-relative origin.

METHOD:: openAction_
Called when Ctrl+left-click is released without becoming a drag. CODE::nil:: clears it. That click does not call LINK::#-clickAction_:: and does not toggle playback.

ARGUMENT:: action
A LINK::Classes/Function:: or CODE::nil::. The function is called with no arguments.

METHOD:: moveTo
Moves the chip so its top-left is CODE::origin::.

ARGUMENT:: origin
A LINK::Classes/Point::.

METHOD:: applyPlaying
Sets the border from CODE::playingId::. The colour is LINK::Classes/GuiPalette#-extreme2:: when CODE::playingId:: is this chip's sequence id, and LINK::Classes/GuiPalette#-colour4:: otherwise.

ARGUMENT:: playingId
A LINK::Classes/Symbol:: or CODE::nil::.

METHOD:: sequenceId
The sequence LINK::Classes/Symbol:: this chip shows.

RETURNS::
A LINK::Classes/Symbol::.

PRIVATE:: prInit, prTogglePlay
